<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Benedict XIV</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1675">1675</a>–<a href="/years/1758">1758</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Prospero Lambertini</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Benedict XIV, born Prospero Lambertini in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bologna">Bologna</a>, was pope from 1740 to 1758 and one of the most learned popes of the 18th century. A noted canon lawyer, he reformed the procedure of canonisation, encouraged scholarship and science and kept good relations with European rulers. In 1751 he suppressed the ancient Patriarchate of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aquileia">Aquileia</a>, dividing its territory between the new archdioceses of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/udine">Udine</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gorizia">Gorizia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/benedict-xiv.jpg" alt="Benedict XIV" width="320" height="422" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pierre Subleyras · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pierre_Subleyras_Portrait_of_Benedict_XIV_1746._Metropolitan_Museum_of_Art.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
